-- title:
--   Switcheroo Point Product Right Left Eq Left Front Point
-- statement:
--   **The reversed-left switcheroo product reduces to the left-front four-factor product.**
--
--   Fix a slice-pair question $q=(x,y)$, a polynomial outcome $g$, and an outcome $o$ of the indexed projective submeasurement. Let
--
--   $$
--   R_{q,g,o}=(M^y_oG^x_g)\otimes I,
--   \qquad
--   L_{q,g,o}=(G^x_gM^y_o)\otimes I.
--   $$
--
--   Then
--
--   $$
--   \operatorname{ev}_{\psi}\!\left(R_{q,g,o}^{\dagger}L_{q,g,o}\right)
--   =
--   \operatorname{ev}_{\psi}\!\left((G^x_gM^y_oG^x_gM^y_o)\otimes I\right).
--   $$
--
--   This is the pointwise left-front scalar identity used in the aggregate switcheroo comparison. It follows by taking the adjoint of the reversed product and preserving the displayed order of the four projection factors.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Pasting.switcherooPointProductRightLeft_eq_leftFront_point`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/LionSR/MIPStarRE/blob/f382c801026f53a9efc260fdee707cb35e0adb15/MIPStarRE/LDT/Pasting/SwitcherooCompletion/Expansion.lean#L221-L267

